# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SubScribe AI — Web build environment
#
# These variables are statically inlined into the web bundle by Vite at build
# time (see vite.config.mjs / the src/utils/webAuth.js imports). They are NOT
# secrets — the Web OAuth flow (Implicit Grant) is designed to run entirely
# client-side without them. Register your app in each provider's console,
# then put ONLY the public Client ID / App Key below.
#
#   • Google Drive  → Google Cloud Console → Credentials → OAuth 2.0 Client ID
#                     (type: "Web application")
#                     Authorized JS origins:  https://<your-domain>   http://localhost:5173
#                     Authorized redirect URIs: https://<your-domain>/   http://localhost:5173/
#
#   • Dropbox       → Dropbox App Console → Scoped app (Full access or App folder)
#                     App key only (no secret needed for web Implicit Grant).
#                     Redirect URIs: https://<your-domain>/   http://localhost:5173/
#
# The DESKTOP build continues to read OAuth secrets from
# electron/cloud/cloud.providers.json (never shipped, gitignored) — nothing
# changes there.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_DROPBOX_APP_KEY=
